  "description": "This course equips students with knowledge of the C/C++ programming language from basic to advanced, *) Basics - C/C++ Keywords, C/C++ Variable Types, Lvalues and Rvalues, Operators in C/C++, Strings, Arrrays, Pointerts, C/C++ References, C/C++ Basic Input/Output ... - OOP *) Advance: C/C++ Standard Template Libaries, Files/streaming ,Exception, template, multithread, smartpointer, etc. *) Skill: Problem-solving thinking skills, logical thinking and technical communication skills in the direction of Computational Thinking (CT).",
  "learning_outcomes": [
    {
      "No.": "1",
      "CLO Name": "CLO1",
      "CLO Details": "Understand and apply fundamental concepts in C/C++ programming, including C/C++ keywords, variable types, Lvalues and Rvalues, operators, strings, arrays, and pointers."
    },
    {
      "No.": "2",
      "CLO Name": "CLO2",
      "CLO Details": "Implement decision-making constructs (if-else, switch), loops (for, while, do-while), and modify program flow using control flow keywords (break, continue, goto)."
    },
    {
      "No.": "3",
      "CLO Name": "CLO3",
      "CLO Details": "Define, declare, and implement functions in C/C++, using modular programming techniques such as recursion, function pointers, and parameter passing."
    },
    {
      "No.": "4",
      "CLO Name": "CLO4",
      "CLO Details": "Understand and apply object-oriented programming (OOP) principles like encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism. Use pointers, references, dynamic memory allocation, and smart pointers in C++ for efficient memory management. Avoid memory leaks and dangling pointers while working with classes, constructors, destructors, templates, and exceptions."
    },
    {
      "No.": "5",
      "CLO Name": "CLO5",
      "CLO Details": "Open, read, write, and close files using C/C++ file handling functions and streams. Distinguish between binary and text file formats and perform random access operations."
    },
    {
      "No.": "6",
      "CLO Name": "CLO6",
      "CLO Details": "Use AI Tools and Computational Thinking (CT) tools to identify, analyze, model, and demonstrate problem-solving"
    }
  ],
